WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:02.940
The Doctor is in... trouble.

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:07.629
The Stephen King adaptation Doctor Sleep,
which functions as a direct sequel to Stanley

00:00:07.629 --> 00:00:12.140
Kubrick's classic The Shining, tanked at the
box office over the Veteran's Day weekend.

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:15.890
The only thing resembling a silver lining:
it wasn't alone.

00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:20.980
The movie, which adapts King's 2013 novel
of the same name, arrived in theaters with

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:22.550
a sterling pedigree.

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:26.300
It was directed by Mike Flanagan, who was
at the helm of the excellent Gerald's Game,

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:30.941
a Netflix original which ported over another
of the master's works to the screen; King

00:00:30.941 --> 00:00:35.450
himself gave Doctor Sleep a ringing endorsement,
and a great many horror fans consider The

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:38.800
Shining to be among the greatest fright flicks
of all time.

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:48.720
"Heeere's Johnny!"

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:53.120
All of these things considered, the story
of a now-adult Danny Torrance still coming

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:57.200
to terms with his unique powers - and the
harrowing events which took place during his

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:02.230
childhood stay at the Overlook Hotel - was
expected to clean up to the tune of $25 to

00:01:02.230 --> 00:01:04.330
$30 million dollars domestic.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:10.470
Shockingly, it came nowhere close to that
total, pulling in an absolutely anemic $14.1

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.400
million dollars at the stateside box office.

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:17.710
It was a disheartening development for studio
Warner Bros., as good reviews and word of

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:21.180
mouth weren't nearly enough to prop up Doctor
Sleep.

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:25.979
The movie was kept out of the weekend's top
spot by Roland Emmerich's historical drama

00:01:25.979 --> 00:01:31.010
Midway, which has received mixed-to-negative
critical notices and claimed victory with

00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:36.790
a $17.5 million haul, which itself is not
exactly impressive.

00:01:36.790 --> 00:01:41.619
Considering that September's It: Chapter Two
underperformed pretty severely for the studio

00:01:41.619 --> 00:01:47.500
compared with its 2017 predecessor, the failure
of Doctor Sleep could be indicative of a trend:

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:52.940
the beginning of the end of the King Renaissance,
which has seen such properties as The Mist,

00:01:52.940 --> 00:01:58.580
Mr. Mercedes, Pet Sematary, and In the Tall
Grass successfully adapted for screens large

00:01:58.580 --> 00:02:01.229
and small in just the last few years.

00:02:01.229 --> 00:02:05.560
A slew of additional King adaptations are
currently in the works, including television

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:11.120
series based on The Stand and Lisey's Story,
and feature films based on Salem's Lot, The

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:13.170
Long Walk, and From a Buick 8.

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:17.230
It should be said that Doctor Sleep might
have had a bit more success if moviegoers

00:02:17.230 --> 00:02:21.930
hadn't inexplicably decided to stay away from
the theater altogether over the weekend.

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:27.120
A little quick math reveals that the top two
movies of Veterans' Day weekend 2019 only

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:31.739
managed about a $32 million dollar domestic
haul, and when we compare and contrast with

00:02:31.739 --> 00:02:35.480
the same weekend in recent years, the difference
is downright eye-popping.

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:40.829
Consider that during the same frame in 2018,
Universal and Illumination's animated feature

00:02:40.829 --> 00:02:47.450
The Grinch topped the box office with a whopping
$67.6 million gross, more than twice the total

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:50.269
that Doctor Sleep and Midway combined for.

00:02:50.269 --> 00:02:55.569
The Freddie Mercury biopic Bohemian Rhapsody
came in second during that frame with $31.2

00:02:55.569 --> 00:03:00.719
million, a respectable total that this year's
top two just barely managed to eclipse.

00:03:00.719 --> 00:03:07.540
In 2017, the top spot went to Thor: Ragnarok
with a $57.1 million haul, and the second

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:12.950
and third spots were filled by Daddy's Home
2 with $29.7 million, and Murder on the Orient

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:15.739
Express with $28.7 million.

00:03:15.739 --> 00:03:19.659
It's plain to see that in each of the last
two years, audiences were all about heading

00:03:19.659 --> 00:03:23.170
out to the multiplex over the Veteran's Day
weekend, and that this year, that trend hit

00:03:23.170 --> 00:03:25.089
a brick wall.

00:03:25.089 --> 00:03:30.699
As noted by The Hollywood Reporter, even Paul
Dergarabedian of Comscore - an analytics company

00:03:30.699 --> 00:03:36.129
which provides marketing data to media and
advertising firms-— remarked that this past

00:03:36.129 --> 00:03:40.150
weekend, quote, "was like some weird alternative
box-office universe."

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:45.260
Unfortunately, it was one in which Doctor
Sleep, by most accounts a very good film and

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:48.739
a very worthy sequel to The Shining, found
itself stuck.

00:03:48.739 --> 00:03:53.401
Hopefully, the flick's jaw-droppingly weak
performance will turn out to be a fluke, as

00:03:53.401 --> 00:03:57.810
year-to-date box office revenue is trailing
significantly behind last year despite the

00:03:57.810 --> 00:04:02.549
stunning success of flicks like Joker - which
is now the most profitable comic book movie

00:04:02.549 --> 00:04:07.480
ever - and Avengers: Endgame, which is simply
the highest-grossing film in history.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:13.010
With such potential smashes as Frozen II and
Star Wars Episode IX: The Rise of Skywalker

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:17.340
still to come, it's certainly not too late
for 2019 to turn it around - but as far as

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:21.769
Doctor Sleep goes, we're calling the time,
because the patient has no pulse.

